- In this thesis: following the narrative of a classical abstract book, we formalize two exercises in finite group theory. By the first exercise, we have transfered the work into an accepted PR in mathlib by generalizing an exisiting theorem in mathlib with some necessary lemmas. By the second exercise, we discuss the gap between formal math and pen-and-paper proof in detail by formalizing the theorems of Hall Subgroup. At last we go deeper the previous discussion by looking at Cauchy's theorem for abelian group, to investigate how commonly used proof techniques—such as induction—behave in a proof assistant setting.

